<!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
<section class="section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Everything you need to know.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does Teamwork Commerce manage product data?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Product information lives in one centralized record — catalog details, variants, images, enrichments, and digital assets. That record is the single source of truth read by POS, e-commerce, marketplaces, and any third-party channel, so the same product looks the same everywhere it appears.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Can product updates be scheduled ahead of a launch?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. You can stage the next version of a product alongside the live one and schedule publishing dates per market, down to the minute. The current version stays released until the scheduled moment, so seasonal changes and drops go live exactly when planned without anyone touching the live record.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What does AI do for product content?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>AI generates product descriptions, translations, search terms, imagery, and video from the record you already have, working within a library of brand messaging so output stays on-brand. It also powers conversational product search for associates and personalized product recommendations they can share with a customer. AI capabilities are a paid upgrade.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does product data reach the point of sale?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The POS reads directly from the same product record rather than a synced copy, so a change to a description, price attribute, or variant is reflected at the register without an integration job. Existing catalog data imports from external systems, and open APIs keep other channels in step.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

